''This week sees a few small tweaks to Deadman: Armageddon and While Guthix Sleeps!''

==Changelog July 24th==
{{Collapsed section|18|CLICK HERE TO SHOW}}
'''Deadman: Armageddon'''

* Significantly increased the rate of the Bleed effect on Morrigan’s Javelin, and increased damage per hit to 10.
* The UI now correctly reflects the remaining time before this year's Deadman ends.
* Removed warning messages that played when players attuned to Sigil of the Fortune Farmer interacted with Impling Jars.
* Increased quantity of Breach NPCs at Region Breaches.
* Updated Slayer Points required to choose a Task when using the Sigil of Slaughter from 30 to 60.
** Players with less than 90 Slayer Points will be warned that they won’t have enough points to cancel a selected Task.
* When attempting to log in to a Deadman world with W45 data, players will now be informed that they must reset their Permanent Deadman account with Nigel in Lumbridge.
* Deadman Tournament accounts, specially one Defence pures, can now progress through Heroes’ Quest. Normal Deadman and other normal accounts remain unchanged.

'''While Guthix Sleeps'''

* Added a consumable teleport to the Guthixian Temple to the tormented demons’ loot table.
* Updated the UI with a new multiway icon which indicates whether players can fight one, two, or three demons at a time.
* Updated Movario's notes, restoring some details from the original RuneScape version. Please note that Old School’s lore means there are still some differences.
* Lucien has had a makeover! He now looks far more formidable.
* Refreshed Laidee Gnonock with updated animations and bulkier armour.
* Updated and added extra dialogue throughout the quest to be more in-keeping with the original, though again you will still see many differences.
* Recoloured the Balance Elemental and the fight with Surok for accessibility.
* Added a chest to Movario’s base which contains the Runes needed for the door puzzle. They will appear there only once.
* Thaerisk will now give out a Snapdragon Seed for free rather than charging for it. He still only gives one.
* Sapphire Lanterns are no longer destroyed on death during the quest.
* Akrisae will now provide a one-time teleport to Ice Mountain for the Black Knight section and will also remind you they need a disguise to enter the fortress.
* When working on the Herblore puzzle in the Guthixian Temple, the corresponding alternate ingredients will now be returned to you. So for example, if you place a herb on a statue that already has one, the first herb will be given back.
* You can now store your Elite Black Armour and the Dark Squall Robes in your Player Owned House.
* Your Broav can now roam free within your Player Owned House!
* The skeletons in Lucien’s camp will now always be aggressive once Lucien has spotted you, regardless of any disguise. They won’t be fooled twice!
* You can now use Runes from your Rune Pouch for the Teleorb.
* All tiles around the Guthixian symbol can now be walked on without issues.
* The Emberlight can now be used for the Master Clue Scroll step as a stand-in for the Arclight, and can be added to your STASH unit.
* Mark of Darkness will now last 5 times longer if the Purging Staff is equipped when cast.
* Players can now forge the Emberlight no matter which items they combine first.
* Elite dark warriors, rangers and mages have been given Melee, Ranged, and Magic Defence stats.
* Updated NPC contact options have been updated to reflect new NPCs.
* The Oneiromancer will now acknowledge a certain NPC’s tragic death.
* Adjusted the consistency of certain NPC chat heads to reflect story progression.
* Flames can now no longer be seen from the floor below during a certain boss fight.
* Resolved a graphical issue affecting Emberlight.

'''Other Changes'''

* The ‘Attack’ option on Zuk is once again visible during the introductory cut scene.
* The Undead Pirates’ lockers in the east of the Wilderness no longer open on non-members worlds.
* Visiting the Trouble Brewing minigame no longer wipes the effect of 'The Stuff' from any vats you've got fermenting.
* Fixed a bug which caused the burning effect from the Eclipse Atlatl and the Burning Claws not to clear upon leaving the Player Owned House Combat Ring. The Burn effect is also now reflected in the buff/debuff bar.
* Akkha, Xarpus and Nylos can now all be affected by burn damage.

'''PvP Rota'''

The PvP rota has moved to '''Period A''':

* 539 - (US) - PvP World
* 318 - (UK) - Bounty Hunter World
* 548 - (Germany) - High-Risk PvP World
* 577 - (US) - Free-to-Play PvP World
* 559 - (UK) - LMS Competitive

World 390 (AUS) for LMS Competitive has been <u>'''activated'''</u> with this rota.

World 569 (AUS) for Bounty Hunter has been <u>'''activated'''</u> with this rota.

The PvP Arena is using '<b>Max/Med</b>' loadouts in Ranked Duels and Tournaments this week.

